  ],
  "policy_implication_not_decided": "RETRACTED 2026-10-04 (round-2 review G1): the earlier text said a deterministic DENY on schema rejection would make both cases correct for any model; see policy_implication_corrected_2026_10_04",
  "policy_implication_corrected_2026_10_04": "DO NOT implement a deterministic DENY on schema rejection until the live request shapes are traced. Static evidence (code read, no runtime trace): every Assistant Orchestrator tool call with arguments carries them under the key args (services/assistant_orchestrator/src/entrypoint.py:401), which validate_parameters_schema rejects; the URL door carries purpose and method, also rejected; such a rule could deny every argument-bearing tool call and every URL fetch if placed where live requests are judged. No production sender of an adjudication request to the model-backed classifier was found; the tool loop and the URL door call DeterministicPolicyChecker in process. Open question for the Lead Architect: is the model path live for argument-bearing requests, and if the model is shown only a rejection marker instead of the arguments, the arguments are judged only by the rule checker (a design question)."
 },
